  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1202.32 Closed molding",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1202.32 “Closed molding” means a fiberglass boat manufacturing process by which pressure is used to distribute a resin through reinforcing fabric placed between 2 mold surfaces to either saturate the fabric or fill the mold cavity. The term includes, but is not limited to, compression molding with sheet molding compound, infusion molding, resin injection molding, vacuum-assisted resin transfer molding, resin transfer molding, and vacuum-assisted compression molding. The term does not include any processes in which a closed mold is used only to compact saturated fabric or remove air or excess resin from the fabric, such as in vacuum bagging.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html"
